  "body": "What happens: `cargo test -p xtask` on current main fails in `gate_maps_tests::no_gate_map_names_a_moved_module_as_app` with `suites without a Gate map: [\"post_script_options\"]`.\n\nExpected: every test-suite file has a Gate map line. The test keeps the map true.\n\nEvidence: the suite `crates/app/tests/post_script_options.rs` came from main (commit ec8fd4b06, PR #258). It has no Gate map line. Found during the independent review of PR #1952 at head 3dbd6f26f: the test function is identical in main and in that head, so the failure belongs to main, not to the PR. The post-merge batch does not run the xtask self-tests, so CI stayed green; a contributor who runs `cargo test -p xtask` sees the red. This repeats #1331 and #1417 (the same test, older suites).\n\nDone means: `post_script_options.rs` carries its Gate map line (the crate and suite name the selector needs), and `cargo test -p xtask gate_maps_tests` is green on main.\n",
